Z||000003||cadero2dmax||12-07-2001||09:22 AM||||I gues nobody has heard of Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory? Not only does he support the Fiero community, but he hosts an annual swap meet where Fiero Lovers from all over the country come on the last weekend in April. You will meet the likes of Rodney Dickman, Dave Held, Paul McKibbon, and others. You can see their displays, and find the most oddball parts out there (15x10 rims for draggin, complete with slicks were GIVEN to the gent parked next to me the year before last).<P>I have a picture of my ex-racer Fiero at his meet on my photopoint site.<P>Ed Parks...from The Fiero Factory<BR>8710B Hwy 53, Toney Ala 35773<BR>Shop..256-420-5391 Hm..256-882-1568 <A HREF="http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory" TARGET=_blank>http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Injected 4.9 Cad powered 85 SE (Daily Driver)5 speed ('88 cradle)<P>86 carburated 4.9 automatic Grassroots Motorsports Magazine $2002 Challenge Fiero coupe (2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit) all on an '88 cradle<P>For Racing Photos of my former Q4 Fiero racecar, go to: <BR>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=142520&a=1342821 <P>(until I can figure out how to post photos)<P>George Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000004||reddog||12-07-2001||11:33 PM||||Look up the Fiero warehouse they have a lot of used items and delivery has always been the quickest that I have seen yet. If you don'tsee the item listed just e-mail him and 9 times out of 10 he will have it!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
